    "body": "# Bug Report\n\n## Description\n\nWhitenoise (a quite popular extension to django) is complaining about a missing css file\n\n## Is this a regression?\n\nYes, it used to work when I was on v1.21.11, now with v1.21.12, I encounter this error.\n\n## Minimal Reproduction\n\nUpgrade to v1.21.12 and use whitenoise and run\n\n> python manage.py collectstatic\n\n## Stack trace / Error message\n\n> whitenoise.storage.MissingFileError: The file 'drf-yasg/swagger-ui-dist/swagger-ui.css.map' could not be found with <whitenoise.storage.CompressedManifestStaticFilesStorage object at 0x79098879d6a0>.\nThe CSS file 'drf-yasg/swagger-ui-dist/swagger-ui.css' references a file which could not be found:\n  drf-yasg/swagger-ui-dist/swagger-ui.css.map\nPlease check the URL references in this CSS file, particularly any\nrelative paths which might be pointing to the wrong location.\n<!-- If the issue is accompanied by an exception or an error, please share it below: -->\n\n## Your Environment\n\n* Python 3.13\n* Django 5.2.10\n* Whitenoise 6.11.0\n",
